 "note": "The circle is horizontal and seen from the side, so the original prints it as an ellipse. The renderer draws only true circles, so the ellipse is 20 dotted chords on semi-axes 170 and 44 - every vertex computed from the ellipse, none placed by hand. The stone sits ON the path and the string runs from the centre to it, so the string is a radius of the circle, which is what the figure is about. The two arrows are tangent to a slightly larger ellipse at 75 and 215 degrees and give the sense of rotation. The grey dot marks where the hand holds the string; the hand itself is not drawable here."
